<title>GERMANY: Buderus acquires Belgium's G.Weckx &amp; Co.</title>
<headline>Buderus acquires Belgium's G.Weckx &amp; Co.</headline>
<dateline>WETZLAR, Germany 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German heating and appliance group Buderus AG said on Friday it had acquired the Belgian firm G. Weckx &amp; Co NV.</p>
<p>Buderus said Weckx had already for 40 years been distributing Buderus products, primarily free-standing oil and gas heating boilers, storage water heaters and contolling equipment.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Buderus said the acquisition would enable it to expand Werckx's distribution to the full range of its products.</p>
<p>Weckx, which has 18 employees, had a 1996 turnover of 12 million marks, the statement said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
